WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.990
You put 1,000 into a savings account.

2
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.300
It pays 5 per cent a year.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.020
A year later, your balance says 1,050.

4
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.200
More money than you started with.

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.570
But the number in an
account is not the same

6
00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.380
as what that money can
actually do for you.

7
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.730
So if your savings grow every year,

8
00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.860
how can you still end up able to buy less?

9
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.320
In this mission, you'll
meet two interest rates:

10
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.220
the one on the bank's sign,

11
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.610
and a hidden one that matters more.

12
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.140
Then you'll work out
who gains and who loses

13
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.890
when a loan agreed today
meets a surprise tomorrow.

14
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.610
Your mission: find out what a
savings rate really tells you.
